  },
  "question": {
    "text": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A particle is moving in one dimension (along <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> axis) under the action of a variable force. It's initial position was <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> right of origin. The variation of its position <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> with time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced></math> is given as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>–</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>18</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo></math> where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math> is in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The velocity of the particle when its acceleration becomes zero is _________ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "52",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>18</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>t</mi></math></p><p>As we know, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>36</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn></math></p><p>Now, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>18</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>36</mn></math></p><p>For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, time till be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math></p><p>Therefore, required velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>36</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>52</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>"
  }
}